Issue #94: Mandatory post-rebuild change safety audit gate

## Goal
After the full stabilization and architecture rebuild are complete, make regression/impact auditing mandatory for every future code change before merge/deploy.

## Policy
Every PR that changes Python/runtime/configuration/workflow behavior must prove that it does not regress already-working functionality. No change may merge solely because its local unit test passes.

## Required per-change audit
For each change, CI must automatically:
- classify the change surface and affected authority boundaries;
- run repository-wide structural/architecture ownership validation;
- run typed-configuration parity and unit-contract validation;
- run canonical state/valuation/accounting/risk/execution invariants relevant to the touched paths;
- run targeted tests for the changed behavior;
- run regression tests for previously proven working behavior whose dependency graph overlaps the change;
- run exact Gunicorn/bootstrap startup smoke;
- block any new mutation owner, route overlap, configuration conflict, import-time activation, unsafe watchdog, silent authoritative exception path, or other architecture-debt increase;
- require explicit evidence that hard risk limits, strategy intent, sizing, live authority, ML execution authority, canonical ledger semantics, and persistence guarantees did not change unless the PR explicitly declares and separately validates such a change;
- produce a machine-readable audit artifact and compact PASS/FAIL summary attached to the PR.

## Merge rule
Post-rebuild, this audit becomes a mandatory branch-protection/status requirement. A PR cannot be merged if the change-safety audit is missing, incomplete, stale relative to the PR head SHA, or failing.

## Acceptance
- one canonical `change_safety_audit` workflow/check is required on all relevant PRs;
- check is tied to the exact PR head SHA;
- impact-aware regression selection plus core invariant suite always runs;
- no bypass through alternate workflow/path-only changes;
- documentation and VALIDATION_POLICY.md define the requirement;
- branch protection / repository rules require the check before merge where connector/repository permissions support it;
- a seeded negative regression proves the gate blocks a breaking change;
- a no-op/safe change proves the gate passes without changing trading behavior.

## Timing
Implement and activate this as the final governance step of the current rebuild program, before declaring the architecture program complete. Until then, existing repository safety, architecture-debt, stage-specific, and startup-smoke gates remain in force.

