- every current non-main branch has an explicit classification;
- active and registered control-plane branches are preserved until safe;
- obsolete branches are deleted normally, never force-moved to `main` or another SHA;
- final branch set is minimal and intentional;
- no production deploy or DB write is required.

## Safety boundary

Classification is read-only. Actual branch deletion requires separate explicit owner authorization after the exact candidate list is presented. No force-push, history rewrite, production deploy, DB/Review write, parser/collector action or RPi5 mutation.

