Issue #2: Maximum call stack size exceeded in monorepos with "." as workspace entry (Yarn Berry)

Description

ts-graph-mcp crashes on startup with a stack overflow in monorepos that use "." as a workspace entry — a standard Yarn Berry pattern where the root package is also a workspace member.

Error


Failed to start HTTP server: RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded
    at findSourceEntry (buildWorkspaceMap.js:229:22)
    at processPackageDirectory (buildWorkspaceMap.js:72:25)
    at processWorkspaceRoot (buildWorkspaceMap.js:51:13)
    at processPackageDirectory (buildWorkspaceMap.js:79:9)
    at processWorkspaceRoot (buildWorkspaceMap.js:51:13)
    ...
Root cause

In buildWorkspaceMap.js, processWorkspaceRoot and processPackageDirectory are mutually recursive with no cycle detection. When the root package.json declares "." as a workspace:


"workspaces": [
  ".",
  "packages/*/*",
  ...
]
The following infinite loop occurs:

processWorkspaceRoot("/repo") → expands glob "." → returns ["/repo"]
processPackageDirectory("/repo") → sees the root package.json has workspaces
→ calls processWorkspaceRoot("/repo") again → infinite recursion
Fix

Pass a visited: Set<string> through the recursive calls and return early if a resolved directory path has already been processed:


export const buildWorkspaceMap = (workspaceRoot) => {
    const result = new Map();
    const visited = new Set();
    processWorkspaceRoot(resolve(workspaceRoot), result, visited);
    return result;
};

const processWorkspaceRoot = (directory, result, visited) => {
    const resolvedDir = resolve(directory);
    if (visited.has(resolvedDir)) return;  // ← break cycle
    visited.add(resolvedDir);
    // ... rest unchanged, pass visited down
};

const processPackageDirectory = (packageDir, result, visited) => {
    const resolvedDir = resolve(packageDir);
    if (visited.has(resolvedDir)) return;  // ← break cycle
    // ... rest unchanged, pass visited down
};
Reproduction

Any Yarn Berry monorepo with "." in its workspaces array (e.g. AFFiNE, many other Yarn 4 projects).

