Issue #15135: Tracking: Minimal Recursive CTE

Recursive CTE (RCTE) is an important feature of SQL, which make the SQL language turing-complete. We don't consider this to be a necessary capability for streaming computing, but while implementing certain iterative algorithms, RCTE is still very useful. We believe that implementing a minimal RCTE under the RisingWave framework is worthwhile.

Abilities that are not supported in the minimal implementation:

* [Mutual Recursion](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mutual_recursion)
* Only `UNION ALL` is supported, we can discuss `UNION` later.
* Parallel iteration calculation inside one epoch will not be supported. In brief, data will be sharded for calculation, but different iterations are calculated one by one.
* At most 16 iterations are supported, and the result set will not extend after 16 iterations.
* While evaluating RCTE in batch mode, the full result may be materialized in the memory and OOM may happen if the result set is large enough.

## Planner

We need support for the Plan Tree with cycles. The simplest approach is to introducing two new operators: `LogicalCteRef` and `LogicalRecursiveUnion`.

![image](https://github.com/risingwavelabs/risingwave/assets/9161438/46d61811-d5d5-4654-b21a-9c9cd5c9e634)


```rust
pub struct LogicalCteRef {
    input: Weak<LogicalRecursiveUnion>,
}
pub struct LogicalRecursiveUnion {
    base: Rc<PlanNode>,
    recursive: Rc<PlanNode>,
}
```

The distribution key of `LogicalCteRef` should be same as its downstream (`LogicalJoin` in the example).

- [ ] Introduce LogicalRecursiveUnion/LogicalCteRef operator 
- [x] #15681

## Stream Planner

The plan is similar to logical plan.

While doing stream key derivation, a new hidden column `iteration smallint` should be added to stream key.

- [ ] Introduce StreamRecursiveUnion/StreamCteRef operator

## Batch Planner

Nothing noticeable

- [ ] Introduce BatchRecursiveUnion/BatchCteRef operator

## Plan Fragmenter

**We don't allow a cycle inside a fragment, so an `Exchange` must be inserted between `RecursiveUnion` to `CteRef`**. If the distribution are same, `NoShuffle` is allowed.

- [ ] handle RCTE in Stream Plan Fragmenter
- [ ] handle RCTE in Batch Plan Fragmenter

## Stream Executor

First, we'll add a new field `iteration: usize` to barrier.

### StreamRecursiveUnion

For `StreamRecursiveUnion`, it should do the following things:

```
downstream: Output
back_cte_ref: Output
iteration = 0;
epoch = undefined;
data = [];
while let message = base.next() {
    match message {
        Barrier => {
            if data.is_empty() || iteration == MAX_RECURSIVE_ITERATION {
                // iteration = 0 represents stop
                back_cte_ref.send(Barrier(iteration = 0));
                // Also tell the downstream all iterations in the epoch have been done.
                downstream.send(Barrier(iteration = 0));
                iteration = 0;
            } else {
                back_cte_ref.send(Barrier(iteration = iteration));
                iteration += 1;
            }
        },
        Record(row) => {
            // Copy and store it
            data.push(row.clone());
            // Also send it to downstream directly, iteration is the hidden column.
            downstream.send(row, iteration = iteration);
        }
    }
}
```

### StreamCteRef

```
upstream: Input
cte_feedback_stream: Input
downstream: Output

loop {
    while let message = upstream.next() {
        match message {
            Barrier(barrier) => break;
            Record(row) => downstream.send(row);
        }
    }
    while let message = cte_feedback_stream {
        match message {
            Barrier(barrier) => {
                if barrier.iteration == 0 { break; }
                else { downstream.send(barrier); }
            }
            Record(row) => downstream.send(row);
        }
    }
}
```

